  "htmlContent": "<p>Up to Artificial Intelligence Notes</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Prompt:</strong> \"Create a graph in mermaid. The graph must be of the type that could clearly indicate the differences and pros and cons of A* over dijkstra. Then perform both algos on it step by step\"\n<strong>Lens Applied:</strong> The Optimizationist</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h1>Algorithm: A* vs. Dijkstra (Heuristic-Guided Search)</h1>\n<h2>1. The Logic (Visual Trace)</h2>\n<p>To visualize the divergence, we use a graph where Dijkstra is forced to explore a \"dead-end\" branch with low edge costs, while A* uses a heuristic to stay on target.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"hljs language-mermaid\">graph LR\n    S((S)) -- 1 --> A((A))\n    A -- 1 --> B((B))\n    B -- 1 --> C((C))\n    S -- 5 --> G((G))\n    C -- 10 --> G\n    \n    style S fill:#f9f,stroke:#333\n    style G fill:#00ff00,stroke:#333\n</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Heuristic values <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> (Distance to G):</strong>\n<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(S)=4, h(A)=10, h(B)=10, h(C)=10, h(G)=0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<h3>Step-by-Step Execution:</h3>\n<p><strong>Dijkstra (Greedy on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>):</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Visit S:</strong> Neighbors A(1), G(5). Open list: <code>{A:1, G:5}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Visit A:</strong> Neighbors B(2). Open list: <code>{B:2, G:5}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Visit B:</strong> Neighbors C(3). Open list: <code>{C:3, G:5}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Visit C:</strong> Neighbors G(13). Open list: <code>{G:5}</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Visit G:</strong> Found path <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S \\to G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> (Cost 5).\n<em>Result:</em> Dijkstra explored the entire <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A-B-C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span> chain because its cumulative cost was lower than the direct <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S \\to G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> edge initially.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><em><em>A</em> (Greedy on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(n) = g(n) + h(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>):</em>*</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Visit S:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(A) = 1 + 10 = 11</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">11</span></span></span></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f(G) = 5 + 0 = 5</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span></li>\n<li>Open list: <code>{G:5, A:11}</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Visit G:</strong> Found path <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S \\to G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">G</span></span></span></span> (Cost 5).\n<em>Result:</em> A* ignored the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A-B-C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span> branch entirely because the heuristic correctly identified that moving towards A increases the total estimated cost.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>2. Complexity Analysis</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">O(E \\log V)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">lo<span style=\"margin-right:0.0139em;\">g</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> for both (using a priority queue). However, A* explores a smaller constant factor of the state space.</li>\n<li><strong>Space:</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">O(V)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">O</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> to store the frontier and visited sets.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>3. Implementation (Optimized)</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"hljs language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">a_star</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">graph, start, goal, h</span>):\n    pq = [(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> + h[start], <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, start, [])] <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># (f, g, node, path)</span>\n    visited = {}\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">while</span> pq:\n        f, g, current, path = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> current == goal: <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> path + [current]\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> current <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> visited <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> visited[current] &#x3C;= g: <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">continue</span>\n        visited[current] = g\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> neighbor, weight <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> graph[current]:\n            new_g = g + weight\n            heapq.heappush(pq, (new_g + h[neighbor], new_g, neighbor, path + [current]))\n</code></pre>\n<h2>4. Edge Cases (The Inversionist)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Inadmissible Heuristic:</strong> If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>></mo><mtext>actual cost</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(n) > \\text{actual cost}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">actual cost</span></span></span></span></span>, A* may return a sub-optimal path (it becomes \"too greedy\").</li>\n<li><strong>Negative Edges:</strong> Both fail; requires Bellman-Ford or SPFA.</li>\n<li><strong>Uniform Heuristic:</strong> If <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">h(n) = 0</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span> for all <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span></span></span></span>, A* collapses into Dijkstra.</li>\n</ul>",
  "rawMarkdown": "\nUp to Artificial Intelligence Notes\n\n> **Prompt:** \"Create a graph in mermaid. The graph must be of the type that could clearly indicate the differences and pros and cons of A* over dijkstra. Then perform both algos on it step by step\"\n> **Lens Applied:** The Optimizationist\n\n# Algorithm: A* vs. Dijkstra (Heuristic-Guided Search)\n\n## 1. The Logic (Visual Trace)\nTo visualize the divergence, we use a graph where Dijkstra is forced to explore a \"dead-end\" branch with low edge costs, while A* uses a heuristic to stay on target.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    S((S)) -- 1 --> A((A))\n    A -- 1 --> B((B))\n    B -- 1 --> C((C))\n    S -- 5 --> G((G))\n    C -- 10 --> G\n    \n    style S fill:#f9f,stroke:#333\n    style G fill:#00ff00,stroke:#333\n```\n\n**Heuristic values $h(n)$ (Distance to G):**\n$h(S)=4, h(A)=10, h(B)=10, h(C)=10, h(G)=0$.\n\n### Step-by-Step Execution:\n**Dijkstra (Greedy on $g(n)$):**\n1. **Visit S:** Neighbors A(1), G(5). Open list: `{A:1, G:5}`.\n2. **Visit A:** Neighbors B(2). Open list: `{B:2, G:5}`.\n3. **Visit B:** Neighbors C(3). Open list: `{C:3, G:5}`.\n4. **Visit C:** Neighbors G(13). Open list: `{G:5}`.\n5. **Visit G:** Found path $S \\to G$ (Cost 5).\n*Result:* Dijkstra explored the entire $A-B-C$ chain because its cumulative cost was lower than the direct $S \\to G$ edge initially.\n\n**A* (Greedy on $f(n) = g(n) + h(n)$):**\n1. **Visit S:** \n   - $f(A) = 1 + 10 = 11$\n   - $f(G) = 5 + 0 = 5$\n   - Open list: `{G:5, A:11}`.\n2. **Visit G:** Found path $S \\to G$ (Cost 5).\n*Result:* A* ignored the $A-B-C$ branch entirely because the heuristic correctly identified that moving towards A increases the total estimated cost.\n\n## 2. Complexity Analysis\n* **Time:** $O(E \\log V)$ for both (using a priority queue). However, A* explores a smaller constant factor of the state space.\n* **Space:** $O(V)$ to store the frontier and visited sets.\n\n## 3. Implementation (Optimized)\n```python\ndef a_star(graph, start, goal, h):\n    pq = [(0 + h[start], 0, start, [])] # (f, g, node, path)\n    visited = {}\n    while pq:\n        f, g, current, path = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        if current == goal: return path + [current]\n        if current in visited and visited[current] <= g: continue\n        visited[current] = g\n        for neighbor, weight in graph[current]:\n            new_g = g + weight\n            heapq.heappush(pq, (new_g + h[neighbor], new_g, neighbor, path + [current]))\n```\n\n## 4. Edge Cases (The Inversionist)\n* **Inadmissible Heuristic:** If $h(n) > \\text{actual cost}$, A* may return a sub-optimal path (it becomes \"too greedy\").\n* **Negative Edges:** Both fail; requires Bellman-Ford or SPFA.\n* **Uniform Heuristic:** If $h(n) = 0$ for all $n$, A* collapses into Dijkstra.\n",
